#{[17592186315485 #edb/ref 1080 "[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 3 \\\\ -4\\end{aligned}]" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186315485 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186315485 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "3fe5d1ab-8253-5b89-a5c0-ca1372be3314" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186315654 #edb/ref 1080 "[\\begin{aligned}6 \\\\ 10 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}]" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186315654 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186315654 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "5f087a9c-6631-5e06-a1ea-ba0a59a17a15" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186315724 #edb/ref 1080 "I and III only" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186315724 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045499 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186315724 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "6b92d802-3085-528a-9c72-efc57cf5c2c4" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186315821 #edb/ref 1080 "None of the statements are true" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186315821 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045499 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186315821 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "800f5135-a705-5bc5-b182-cd0428d00e1a" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186315941 #edb/ref 1080 "I and II only" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186315941 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045499 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186315941 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "93c3185c-8c40-5110-addf-07d04037df9e" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186316109 #edb/ref 1080 "[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ -10 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186316109 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186316109 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "ae94241c-5c88-5581-8a78-e3b6112151f6" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186316627 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186315321 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186316627 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186315451 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186316627 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186315724 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186316627 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186315821 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186316627 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186315941 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186316627 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186316627 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186316627 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186315451 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186316627 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "22bb0e27-d6d9-5966-9fb5-317681ddbc7c" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186316711 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186315249 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186316711 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186315397 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186316711 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186315485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186316711 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186315654 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186316711 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186316109 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186316711 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186316711 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186316711 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186315485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186316711 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "483bd6df-6359-5977-8496-d54fb13d179d" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186317317 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186316711 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186317317 #edb/ref 1069 "q-34271" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186317317 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186317317 #edb/ref 1071 "The set ${{a}_{1},{a}_{2}}$ is linearly dependent. Which of the following vectors could be ${a}_{2}$ if\n${a}_{1}=[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ -6 \\\\ 8\\end{aligned}]?$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186317317 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "62d9b5f5-3d93-555f-bd13-2fa9aa2fe12b" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186317317 #edb/ref 1074 "We say that two vectors ${v}_{1}$ and ${v}_{2}$ are *linearly independent* if the only solution to the equation\n\n$$\n{x}_{1}{v}_{1}+{x}_{2}{v}_{2}=0\n$$\n\nis ${x}_{1}={x}_{2}=0.$ Otherwise, the vectors are *linearly dependent*.\n\nA set containing *only two* vectors is linearly *dependent* if and only if the two vectors are parallel.\n\nFrom the given options, the correct answer is\n\n$$\n{a}_{2}=[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 3 \\\\ -4\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nTo see why, notice that \n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 3 \\\\ -4\\end{aligned}]=-\\frac{1}{2}[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ -6 \\\\ 8\\end{aligned}]=-\\frac{1}{2}{a}_{1}.\n$$\n\nThis way, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{2}{a}_{1}-\\frac{1}{2}{a}_{1} & =0 \\\\ \\frac{1}{2}{a}_{1}+{a}_{2} & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIn other words, the vectors ${a}_{1}$ and ${a}_{2}$ are parallel.\n\nTo see why this means that ${a}_{1}$ and ${a}_{2}$ are linearly dependent, we notice that the equation\n\n$$\n{x}_{1}{a}_{1}+{x}_{2}{a}_{2}=0\n$$\n\nhas the solution ${x}_{1}=\\frac{1}{2}$ and ${x}_{2}=1,$ which is different from ${x}_{1}={x}_{2}=0.$ Therefore, the set is linearly dependent." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186317320 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186316627 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186317320 #edb/ref 1069 "q-34276" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186317320 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186317320 #edb/ref 1071 "Consider the following vectors:\n\n$$\n{a}_{1}=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}],\\,{a}_{2}=[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}],\\,{a}_{3}=[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ -1 \\\\ -4\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nAssume that ${x}_{1},{x}_{2},$ and ${x}_{3}$ are real numbers. Which of the following statements are true?\n\nI. The equation ${x}_{1}{a}_{1}+{x}_{2}{a}_{2}+{x}_{3}{a}_{3}=0$ has only the trivial solution ${x}_{1}={x}_{2}={x}_{3}=0.$\n\nII. The vectors ${a}_{1},{a}_{2},$ and ${a}_{3}$ are linearly independent.\n\nIII. The vectors ${a}_{1},{a}_{2},$ and ${a}_{3}$ are linearly dependent." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186317320 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "1120ac93-1146-5212-b323-41cae9ac4014" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186317320 #edb/ref 1074 "We say that three vectors ${v}_{1},{v}_{2},$ and ${v}_{3}$ are *linearly independent* if the only solution to the equation\n\n$$\n{x}_{1}{v}_{1}+{x}_{2}{v}_{2}+{x}_{3}{v}_{3}=0\n$$\n\nis ${x}_{1}={x}_{2}={x}_{3}=0.$ Otherwise, the vectors are *linearly dependent*.\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine our statements.\n\nThe equation ${x}_{1}{a}_{1}+{x}_{2}{a}_{2}+{x}_{3}{a}_{3}=0$ corresponds to the system\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}-2{x}_{2}+3{x}_{3}=0 \\\\ {x}_{2}-{x}_{3}=0 \\\\ -3{x}_{1}+{x}_{2}-4{x}_{3}=0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo solve the system, we create its augmented matrix and reduce it using Gaussian elimination:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 & 3 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -1 & 0 \\\\ -3 & 1 & -4 & 0\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+3{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 & 3 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -5 & 5 & 0\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+5{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 & 3 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the matrix above, we conclude that the basic variables are ${x}_{1}$ and ${x}_{2}$, while ${x}_{3}$ is the free variable. \n\nSince there is one free variable, the equation ${x}_{1}{a}_{1}+{x}_{2}{a}_{2}+{x}_{3}{a}_{3}=0$ has an infinite number of nonzero solutions, which means that the vectors are linearly dependent. \n\nTherefore, statements I and II are false, while statement III is true." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186342393 #edb/ref 1080 "None of the statements are true" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186342393 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045499 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186342393 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "11972855-80a9-5cac-9e70-8a4fcbdccf24" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186342608 #edb/ref 1080 "I and III only" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186342608 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045499 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186342608 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "2bfeba34-6da2-5961-afdc-9d9564e3b098" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186342746 #edb/ref 1080 "I and II only" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186342746 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045499 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186342746 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "3da42d