 17592186343789 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186344686 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186344432 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186344686 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186344488 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186344686 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186344686 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186344686 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186343789 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186344686 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "6c97eb9a-a992-5953-a80c-a71608c9beca" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186344852 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186342393 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186344852 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186342608 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186344852 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186343756 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186344852 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186343758 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186344852 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186344433 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186344852 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186344852 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186344852 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186343756 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186344852 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "d156fe28-1c7f-5127-9119-2df01429f973" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186345113 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186344686 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186345113 #edb/ref 1069 "q-75659" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186345113 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045486 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186345113 #edb/ref 1071 "Consider the following vectors:\n\n$$\n{a}_{1}=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}],\\,{a}_{2}=[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 2 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}],\\,{a}_{3}=[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\n \n\nAssume that ${x}_{1},{x}_{2},$ and ${x}_{3}$ are real numbers. Which of the following statements are true?\n\n- The vectors ${a}_{1},{a}_{2},$ and ${a}_{3}$ are linearly dependent.\n- The equation ${x}_{1}{a}_{1}+{x}_{2}{a}_{2}+{x}_{3}{a}_{3}=0$ has only the trivial solution ${x}_{1}={x}_{2}={x}_{3}=0.$\n- The vectors ${a}_{1},{a}_{2},$ and ${a}_{3}$ are linearly independent." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186345113 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "0d48ab70-ab46-5142-a432-382f1feb7bb9" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186345113 #edb/ref 1074 "We say that three vectors ${v}_{1},{v}_{2},$ and ${v}_{3}$ are *linearly independent* if the only solution to the equation\n\n$$\n{x}_{1}{v}_{1}+{x}_{2}{v}_{2}+{x}_{3}{v}_{3}=0\n$$\n\nis ${x}_{1}={x}_{2}={x}_{3}=0.$ Otherwise, the vectors are *linearly dependent*.\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine our statements.\n\nThe equation ${x}_{1}{a}_{1}+{x}_{2}{a}_{2}+{x}_{3}{a}_{3}=0$ corresponds to the system \n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}-{x}_{2}=0 \\\\ -{x}_{1}+2{x}_{2}-2{x}_{3}=0 \\\\ 2{x}_{1}-2{x}_{2}+{x}_{3}=0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo solve the system, we create its augmented matrix and reduce it using Gaussian elimination:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ -1 & 2 & -2 & 0 \\\\ 2 & -2 & 1 & 0\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -2 & 0 \\\\ 2 & -2 & 1 & 0\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+(-2){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 0\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the system is now\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}-{x}_{2}=0 \\\\ {x}_{2}-2{x}_{3}=0 \\\\ {x}_{3}=0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the third equation, we get ${x}_{3}=0.$ Substituting this into the second equation, we get\n\n$$\n{x}_{2}-2(0)=0\\,⟹\\,{x}_{2}=0\n$$\n\nand, substituting this into the first equation, we obtain\n\n$$\n{x}_{1}-(0)=0\\,⟹\\,{x}_{1}=0.\n$$\n\nSince ${x}_{1}={x}_{2}={x}_{3}=0$, we get that the set ${{a}_{1},{a}_{2},{a}_{3}}$ is linearly independent.\n\nTherefore, statements II and III are true, while statement I is false." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186345114 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186344852 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186345114 #edb/ref 1069 "q-75660" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186345114 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045486 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186345114 #edb/ref 1071 "Consider the following vectors:\n\n$$\n{a}_{1}=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -4 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}],\\,{a}_{2}=[\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ 13 \\\\ 9\\end{aligned}],\\,{a}_{3}=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -7 \\\\ -4\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\n \n\nAssume that ${x}_{1},{x}_{2},$ and ${x}_{3}$ are real numbers. Which of the following statements are true?\n\n- The vectors ${a}_{1},{a}_{2},$ and ${a}_{3}$ are linearly independent.\n- The vectors ${a}_{1},{a}_{2},$ and ${a}_{3}$ are linearly dependent.\n- The equation ${x}_{1}{a}_{1}+{x}_{2}{a}_{2}+{x}_{3}{a}_{3}=0$ has an infinite number of nonzero solutions." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186345114 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "8d177800-f6a6-59b3-bf6e-5adc772e358a" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186345114 #edb/ref 1074 "We say that three vectors ${v}_{1},{v}_{2},$ and ${v}_{3}$ are *linearly independent* if the only solution to the equation\n\n$$\n{x}_{1}{v}_{1}+{x}_{2}{v}_{2}+{x}_{3}{v}_{3}=0\n$$\n\nis ${x}_{1}={x}_{2}={x}_{3}=0.$ Otherwise, the vectors are *linearly dependent*.\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine our statements.\n\nThe equation ${x}_{1}{a}_{1}+{x}_{2}{a}_{2}+{x}_{3}{a}_{3}=0$ corresponds to the system \n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}-3{x}_{2}+2{x}_{3}=0 \\\\ -4{x}_{1}+13{x}_{2}-7{x}_{3}=0 \\\\ -3{x}_{1}+9{x}_{2}-4{x}_{3}=0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo solve the system, we create its augmented matrix and reduce it using Gaussian elimination:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & -3 & 2 & 0 \\\\ -4 & 13 & -7 & 0 \\\\ -3 & 9 & -4 & 0\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+4{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -3 & 2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1 & 0 \\\\ -3 & 9 & -4 & 0\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+3{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -3 & 2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 2 & 0\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the system is now\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}-3{x}_{2}+2{x}_{3}=0 \\\\ {x}_{2}+{x}_{3}=0 \\\\ 2{x}_{3}=0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the third equation, we get ${x}_{3}=0.$ Substituting this into the second equation, we get\n\n$$\n{x}_{2}+(0)=0\\,⟹\\,{x}_{2}=0\n$$\n\nand, substituting this into the first equation, we obtain\n\n$$\n{x}_{1}-3(0)+2(0)=0\\,⟹\\,{x}_{1}=0.\n$$\n\nSince ${x}_{1}={x}_{2}={x}_{3}=0$, we get that the set ${{a}_{1},{a}_{2},{a}_{3}}$ is linearly independent.\n\nTherefore, statements II and III are false, while statement I is true." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186396585 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186396586 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186396585 #edb/ref 1069 "q-105291" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186396585 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186396585 #edb/ref 1071 "The set $\\{{a}_{1},{a}_{2}\\}$ is linearly dependent. Which of the following vectors could be ${a}_{2}$ if\n${a}_{1}=[\\begin{aligned}9 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}]?$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186396585 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "faa7ddb4-5b88-5e56-a53e-35fdb9d2ef93" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186396585 #edb/ref 1074 "We say that two vectors ${v}_{1}$ and ${v}_{2}$ are *linearly independent* if the only solution to the equation\n\n$$\n{x}_{1}{v}_{1}+{x}_{2}{v}_{2}=0\n$$\n\nis ${x}_{1}={x}_{2}=0.$ Otherwise, the vectors are *linearly dependent*.\n\nA set containing *only two* vectors is linearly *dependent* if and only if the two vectors are parallel.\n\nFrom the given options, the correct answer is \n\n$$\n{a}_{2}=[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nTo see why, notice that \n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]=\\frac{1}{3}[\\begin{aligned}9 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}]=\\frac{1}{3}{a}_{1}.\n$$\n\nThis way, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{3}{a}_{1}-\\frac{1}{3}{a}_{1} & =0 \\\\ \\frac{1}{3}{a}_{1}-{a}_{2} & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIn other words, the vectors ${a}_{1}$ and ${a}_{2}$ are parallel.\n\nTo see why this means that ${a}_{1}$ and ${a}_{2}$ are linearly dependent, we notice that the equation\n\n$$\n{x}_{1}{a}_{1}+{x}_{2}{a}_{2}=0\n$$\n\nhas the solution ${x}_{1}=\\frac{1}{3}$ and ${x}_{2}=-1,$ which is different from ${x}_{1}={x}_{2}=0.$ Therefore, the set is linearly dependent." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186396586 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186396587 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186396586 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186396588 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186396586 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186396589 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186396586 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186396590 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186396586 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186396591 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186396586 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186396586 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186396586 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186396590 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186396586 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "a01010bc-5e11-583a-98fc-7b20994c0fc5" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186396587 #edb/ref 1080 "[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}]" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186396587 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186396587 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "e5f3b240-c702-580d-9cdf-43123253f773" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186396588 #edb/ref 1080 "[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186396588 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186396588 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "574dea89-ee9d-5556-a72b-c257c732699e" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186396589 #edb/ref 1080 "[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}]" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186396589 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186396589 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "640a91d9-57f7-5e99-bc15-29e1456e8af0" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186396590 #edb/ref 1080 "[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186396590 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186396590 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "2044901